// Automatic updates (unattended-upgrades) also install FlickOS's own packages,
// the community apps and the apps bought from FlickOS's store: this adds
// FlickOS's three distributions to the origins that Debian's
// 50unattended-upgrades allows. Shipped by flickos-archive-keyring, with the
// repository itself (sources.list.d/flickos.sources); origin, codename and
// label are the distributions' own (repo/conf/distributions, and the store's
// server/store/new-repo.sh). Community apps update this
// way because every version is built from public source, checked and
// reviewed before it is signed (Software design, Q10). The store's matches
// nothing until its key is added (flickos-control purchases, which writes its
// sources entry; docs/design/flickos-store.md, ADR-004).
//
// Settings > Updates (flickos-control) replaces the whole list in
// 60flickos-updates when a choice is made there, so this file then no longer
// counts; "Security fixes only" leaves FlickOS out.
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=FlickOS,codename=${distro_codename},label=FlickOS";
        "origin=FlickOS,codename=${distro_codename}-community,label=FlickOS Community";
        "origin=FlickOS,codename=${distro_codename}-store,label=FlickOS Store";
};
